<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 01:20:01 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>为了找回被纳粹掠夺的艺术品，研究人员正在发挥创意，采取新策略，包括人工智能聊天机器人和“通缉”海报活动</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/to-recover-artworks-looted-by-the-nazis-researchers-are-getting-creative-with-new-strategies-including-an-ai-chatbot-and-a-campaign-of-wanted-posters-180989247/</link><description>大学研究人员希望他们的新人工智能聊天机器人使来源研究变得更容易、更容易</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:33:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/to-recover-artworks-looted-by-the-nazis-researchers-are-getting-creative-with-new-strategies-including-an-ai-chatbot-and-a-campaign-of-wanted-posters-180989247/</guid></item><item><title>新图像提供了迄今为止最好的证据，证明超巨星参宿四确实有一个长期理论化的恒星伴星</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-images-provide-the-best-evidence-yet-that-supergiant-star-betelgeuse-does-inded-have-a-long-theorized-stellar-companion-180989225/</link><description>研究团队对这些数据基本信服，但他们希望在 2027 年捕获更多观察结果以证实他们的发现</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 20:07:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-images-provide-the-best-evidence-yet-that-supergiant-star-betelgeuse-does-inded-have-a-long-theorized-stellar-companion-180989225/</guid></item><item><title>这座拥有 400 年历史、坚不可摧的日本城堡在武士围攻中幸存下来，刚刚在地震中倒塌</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-400-year-old-impenetrable-japanese-castle-that-survived-a-samurai-siege-just-crumbled-in-an-earthquake-180989248/</link><description>1877年，一支反抗明治天皇的军队袭击了日本南部九州岛的熊本城</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:55:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-400-year-old-impenetrable-japanese-castle-that-survived-a-samurai-siege-just-crumbled-in-an-earthquake-180989248/</guid></item><item><title>一名男子将这件内战文物用作办公桌上的镇纸。拆弹小组告诉他这实际上是一枚实弹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-man-used-this-civil-war-artifact-as-a-paperweight-on-his-desk-the-bomb-squad-told-him-it-was-actually-a-live-explosive-180989245/</link><description>该装置原来是 1800 年代中期为帕罗特步枪设计的炮弹。专家在圣安东尼奥附近的射击场安全引爆了它</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:40:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-man-used-this-civil-war-artifact-as-a-paperweight-on-his-desk-the-bomb-squad-told-him-it-was-actually-a-live-explosive-180989245/</guid></item><item><title>一名患有罕见遗传疾病的青少年在接受定制实验药物后首次独立行走</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/after-receiving-a-custom-experimental-medicine-a-teen-with-a-rare-genetic-disorder-walked-on-his-own-for-the-first-time-180989230/</link><description>患者的遗传性疾病导致频繁癫痫发作和发育迟缓。他的进步以及另一个接受类似个性化治疗的男孩的进步凸显了定制药物的前景和挑战</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:31:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/after-receiving-a-custom-experimental-medicine-a-teen-with-a-rare-genetic-disorder-walked-on-his-own-for-the-first-time-180989230/</guid></item><item><title>智利发现的木乃伊中隐藏了数百年的天花 DNA 表明欧洲殖民者将这种病毒带到了美洲</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/smallpox-dna-hidden-for-centuries-in-mummies-found-in-chile-suggests-european-colonists-brought-the-virus-to-the-americas-180989244/</link><description>研究人员表示，他们发现了病毒致命轨迹的第一个直接分子证据</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:27:18 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/smallpox-dna-hidden-for-centuries-in-mummies-found-in-chile-suggests-european-colonists-brought-the-virus-to-the-americas-180989244/</guid></item><item><title>这个人把人类尸体变成了受欢迎的博物馆展品。现在，这些有争议的“身体世界”的创造者将自己的身体捐赠给了科学</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-man-turned-human-corpses-into-popular-museum-displays-now-the-creator-of-these-controversial-body-worlds-has-donated-his-own-body-to-science-180989242/</link><description>冈瑟·冯·哈根斯 (Gunther von Hagens) 发明了塑化术，这是一种通过用聚合物代替天然液体来保存尸体的方法，最近去世，享年 81 岁</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:56:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-man-turned-human-corpses-into-popular-museum-displays-now-the-creator-of-these-controversial-body-worlds-has-donated-his-own-body-to-science-180989242/</guid></item><item><title>稀有化石揭示了时间冻结的三层食物链：翼龙被鱼龙吃掉，上龙又被吃掉</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rare-fossil-reveals-a-three-tier-food-chain-frozen-in-time-a-pterosaur-eaten-by-an-ichthyosaur-eaten-by-a-pliosaur-180989243/</link><description>该化石由澳大利亚业余化石猎人部分发现，保留了史前捕食动态的独特面貌</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:40:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rare-fossil-reveals-a-three-tier-food-chain-frozen-in-time-a-pterosaur-eaten-by-an-ichthyosaur-eaten-by-a-pliosaur-180989243/</guid></item><item><title>在 2028 年夏季奥运会之前，洛杉矶标志性的瓦茨塔将获得 2200 万美元的校园扩建</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-iconic-watts-towers-in-los-angeles-will-get-a-22-million-campus-expansion-ahead-of-the-2028-summer-olympics-180989240/</link><description>占地 5 英亩的绿地将环绕这座由 17 栋建筑组成的地标建筑，这是一位意大利移民花费三十年时间建造的民间艺术杰作</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:05:19 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-iconic-watts-towers-in-los-angeles-will-get-a-22-million-campus-expansion-ahead-of-the-2028-summer-olympics-180989240/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家发现两座缩略图大小的鸟类雕塑，由 4 万年前的猛犸象牙雕刻而成</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-discover-two-thumbnail-sized-bird-sculptures-carved-from-mammoth-ivory-40000-years-ago-180989239/</link><description>这些雕像长不到一英寸，埋在德国霍勒费尔斯洞穴下方，那里发现了一些世界上最古老的已知雕像艺术品</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:01:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-discover-two-thumbnail-sized-bird-sculptures-carved-from-mammoth-ivory-40000-years-ago-180989239/</guid></item><item><title>古代DNA表明，冰河时代的人类大多杀死了雌性猛犸象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ice-age-humans-mostly-killed-female-woolly-mammoths-suggests-ancient-dna-180989241/</link><description>在分析了 500 多块猛犸象骨骼后，研究人员发现，古代人类过度捕猎雌性猛犸象，原因尚不清楚</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:41:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ice-age-humans-mostly-killed-female-woolly-mammoths-suggests-ancient-dna-180989241/</guid></item><item><title>南极内部气温降至零下 119.4 华氏度，这是十多年来地球有记录以来的最低温度</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/antarctic-interior-hits-119-4-degrees-fahrenheit-earths-lowest-recorded-temperature-in-more-than-a-decade-180989231/</link><description>康科迪亚研究站创纪录的寒冷发生在几周前，最南端大陆的另一个地区经历了相反的极端情况，冬季气温攀升至前所未有的高位</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/antarctic-interior-hits-119-4-degrees-fahrenheit-earths-lowest-recorded-temperature-in-more-than-a-decade-180989231/</guid></item><item><title>隐藏在亚马逊树冠下的神秘形状揭示了一个庞大的古代文明，其规模比研究人员预期的要大得多</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysterious-shapes-hidden-beneath-the-amazon-canopy-reveal-a-sprawling-ancient-civilization-much-bigger-than-researchers-expected-180989236/</link><description>科学家最近在巴西北部发现了数百个来自阿奎里文明的巨大几何土方工程，被称为“地画”</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:47:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysterious-shapes-hidden-beneath-the-amazon-canopy-reveal-a-sprawling-ancient-civilization-much-bigger-than-researchers-expected-180989236/</guid></item><item><title>音频工程师在先锋“蓝调之母”的新歌曲宝库中恢复了隐藏的音符并揭示了丢失的乐器</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/audio-engineers-restored-hidden-notes-and-revealed-lost-instruments-in-this-new-treasure-trove-of-songs-by-the-pioneering-mother-of-the-blues-180989228/</link><description>该专辑收录了 118 首曲目，是美国蓝调偶像 Ma Rainey 录制的最完整的一套唱片</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 20:14:54 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/audio-engineers-restored-hidden-notes-and-revealed-lost-instruments-in-this-new-treasure-trove-of-songs-by-the-pioneering-mother-of-the-blues-180989228/</guid></item><item><title>一种奇怪的、前所未见的癌症似乎正在新英格兰湖的鲶鱼中传播</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-strange-never-before-seen-cancer-seems-to-be-spreading-among-catfish-in-a-new-england-lake-180989195/</link><description>十多年前，渔民和生物学家注意到门弗雷梅戈格湖的棕色牛头鲶鱼的皮肤上有乌黑的肿瘤。基因测试暗示它们是由鱼类中记录的第一种传染性癌症引起的</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:40:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-strange-never-before-seen-cancer-seems-to-be-spreading-among-catfish-in-a-new-england-lake-180989195/</guid></item><item><title>危险的“火云”使法国野火更具破坏性</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/dangerous-fire-clouds-are-making-frances-wildfires-even-more-destructive-180989234/</link><description>这种在北美相当普遍的现象在法国还是第一次出现</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:14:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/dangerous-fire-clouds-are-making-frances-wildfires-even-more-destructive-180989234/</guid></item><item><title>想与巨石阵共度独处时光吗？今年八月，幸运的游客有机会在向游客开放之前进入石圈</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/want-to-spend-some-alone-time-with-stonehenge-this-august-lucky-visitors-get-the-chance-to-enter-the-stone-circle-before-the-site-opens-to-tourists-180989229/</link><description>下个月几乎每天，英格兰史前地标的管理人员都会抽出一张中奖彩票，并在每日忙碌开始之前为游客提供独特的体验</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:02:41 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/want-to-spend-some-alone-time-with-stonehenge-this-august-lucky-visitors-get-the-chance-to-enter-the-stone-circle-before-the-site-opens-to-tourists-180989229/</guid></item><item><title>一名男子发现了一个从地面直立的神秘金属物体。原来是一把2700年历史的宝剑</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-man-unearthed-a-mysterious-metal-object-sticking-straight-up-from-the-ground-it-turned-out-to-be-a-2700-year-old-sword-180989232/</link><description>马尔钦·维希涅夫斯基 (Marcin Wiśniewski) 在波兰格但斯克市附近的森林中进行金属探测时发现了这把武器。专家告诉他，这可能可以追溯到公元前 900 年至 700 年之间</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:01:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-man-unearthed-a-mysterious-metal-object-sticking-straight-up-from-the-ground-it-turned-out-to-be-a-2700-year-old-sword-180989232/</guid></item><item><title>新研究表明，长期暴露于道路交通噪音可能会增加患帕金森病的风险</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/long-term-exposure-to-road-traffic-noise-might-increase-your-risk-of-developing-parkinsons-disease-new-research-suggests-180989216/</link><description>一项研究在 18 年间对丹麦 310 万成年人进行了调查，发现存在适度但一致的相关性。研究结果表明，破坏性的环境声音是脑部疾病的一个可靠的危险因素</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:30:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/long-term-exposure-to-road-traffic-noise-might-increase-your-risk-of-developing-parkinsons-disease-new-research-suggests-180989216/</guid></item><item><title>毁灭恐龙的小行星撞击可能已将我们的星球变成了地狱般的地狱，在数小时内烧焦了大多数生物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-dino-killing-asteroid-strike-may-have-transformed-our-planet-into-a-hellish-inferno-charbroiling-most-creatures-within-hours-180989226/</link><description>根据计算机模拟和地质证据，科学家们提出，这场致命事件可能导致了全球野火和大气中滞留的热量，烤焦了任何无法足够快地躲避的动物</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-dino-killing-asteroid-strike-may-have-transformed-our-planet-into-a-hellish-inferno-charbroiling-most-creatures-within-hours-180989226/</guid></item></channel></rss>